{title: Come Thou Fount of Every Blessing}
{artist: Robert Robinson / John Wyeth (Nettleton)}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Opening, Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: D}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 28장}
{title_ko: 복의 근원 강림하사}
{score: come-thou-fount.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Come, Thou Fount of [G]every [D]blessing
Tune my [Bm]heart to [A]sing Thy [D]grace
[D]Streams of mercy, [G]never [D]ceasing
Call for [Bm]songs of [A]loudest [D]praise
Teach me some me[G]lodious [D]sonnet
Sung by [Bm]flaming [A]tongues a[D]bove
[D]Praise the mount, I'm [G]fixed up[D]on it
Mount of [A]Thy re[G]deeming [D]love
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Here I raise mine [G]Eben[D]ezer
Hither [Bm]by Thy [A]help I'm [D]come
[D]And I hope, by [G]Thy good [D]pleasure
Safely [Bm]to ar[A]rive at [D]home
Jesus [G]sought me when a [D]stranger
Wandering [Bm]from the [A]fold of [D]God
[D]He, to rescue [G]me from [D]danger
Interposed His [A]precious [G]blood [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]O to grace how [G]great a [D]debtor
Daily [Bm]I'm con[A]strained to [D]be
[D]Let Thy goodness, [G]like a [D]fetter
Bind my [Bm]wandering [A]heart to [D]Thee
Prone to [G]wander, Lord, I [D]feel it
Prone to [Bm]leave the [A]God I [D]love
[D]Here's my heart, O [G]take and [D]seal it
Seal it [A]for Thy [G]courts a[D]bove
{end_of_verse}
